; iter_short_stack_int_register: ITER pops both operands before it reads its
; register, so a short stack raises StackUnderflow even when the register
; would also have been rejected.
;
; spec/xqvm/ISA.md's ITER row orders the steps "Pop `end_idx`, then
; `start_idx`. Read vec from `reg`", and spec/xqvm/SPEC.md's error-precedence
; rule makes operand pops first within every instruction. Resolving the
; register first would raise TYPE_MISMATCH here instead of STACK_UNDERFLOW.
;
; The register is filled from calldata rather than left unset so that the
; only fault available to the register arm is a type mismatch: an unset
; register would raise UNSET_REGISTER (see iter_unset_register) and would
; not discriminate the pop order.
;
; One value is pushed where ITER needs two.

PUSH 0
INPUT r0         ; r0 = 5, an int
PUSH 1           ; one operand where ITER pops two
ITER r0
NEXT

PUSH 7
STOW r1
PUSH 0
OUTPUT r1
HALT
